The first one I wanna talk about for this post is a vocaloid singer with a lot of heart and who could be Boyfriend’s sister
Hatsune Miku, although not strictly canon to JUST the FNF universe, has one of the best mods ever made, coming from who recently played it
If you couldn’t tell by now, I’m actually playing the mods for the game, the old ones mainly, but I did v3.0 of Wii Funkin, 
and lemme tell ya, it is extremely difficult
Anyways, back to Miku stuff, I appreciate her style and flow of singing, and I wish to see it more often in today’s media
It does kinda also fit the FNF singing style, what with them both using auto-tuned voices that sound incredible

The next mod character I wanna talk about is a certain bunny rabbit who loves getting herself into trouble
Skarlet Bunny from the Graffiti Groovin’ mod might just one of the best anthropomorphized humans yet
I haven’t played her mod yet, but it’s certainly on my to-do list
She has such a can-do attitude and looks ready for just about anything
She also looks like she might swindle out of your life savings, but you’ll forgive, after all, she’s so cute

The final mod character on today’s list (and final overall) is sorta a joke character created to mock the “Whitty” style of mod progression
I’m talking about Bob from “Literally every FNF mod ever”, the white blob who looks kinda like Dream and is not afraid to go demon mode if you beat him twice
I haven’t been Bob’s Onslaught, but I have dabbled a lot in the original mod, and lemme just say, Run is actually very difficult
Bob is just one lovable guy, has a simplistic and cute design, and could probably be inserted into any social scenario, given personality cues

